65,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,46254,57960,15940,61,18,220,16,23,24884,43298,488,1124,15940,61,17,220,16,23,24884,43298,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nCompute $\\sin^3 18^\\circ + \\sin^2 18^\\circ.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9d470541f545be1dd07427d4a669227857c0ebae31d4570793c53ba4ce748a54"},"seconds":16.4167742729187,"seed":924418116378724515,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem \\(\\sin^3 18^\\circ + \\sin^2 18^\\circ\\), we start by letting \\(x = \\sin 18^\\circ\\). This transforms the expression into \\(x^3 + x^2\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the value of \\(\\sin 18^\\circ\\). It is well-known that \\(\\sin 18^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\). We can verify this using the fact that \\(18^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi}{10}\\), and the properties of the pentagon and the golden ratio. However, for the purpose of this problem, we will use this known value directly.\n\nNow, we substitute \\(x = \\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\) into the expression \\(x^3 + x^2\\):\n\n\\[\nx^3 + x^2 = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^3 + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^2\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^2\\):\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{(\\sqrt{5} - 1)^2}{16} = \\frac{5 - 2\\sqrt{5} + 1}{16} = \\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt{5}}{16} = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{8}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^3\\):\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4}\\right)^3 = \\frac{(\\sqrt{5} - 1)^3}{64} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{5} - 1)(5 - 2\\sqrt{5} + 1)}{64} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{5} - 1)(6 - 2\\sqrt{5})}{64} = \\frac{6\\sqrt{5} - 10 - 6 + 2\\sqrt{5}}{64} = \\frac{8\\sqrt{5} - 16}{64} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 2}{8}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two results together:\n\n\\[\nx^3 + x^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 2}{8} + \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{8} = \\frac{(\\sqrt{5} - 2) + (3 - \\sqrt{5})}{8} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\sin^3 18^\\circ + \\sin^2 18^\\circ\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:407"}
